  "notProven": [
    "The detector proposes compact contrast peaks of the chosen hue; it cannot tell a lantern from a bright flower, sign, window row, wet-floor glint or reflection outside the stage's ground and water, and it misses a lamp no brighter than its surroundings. Look at lights-overlay.png, edit lights.json and re-bake it with the cookie verb.",
    "Positions are glow centroids: a glow cut by an occluder or the plate edge pulls its centre.",
    "Colour is the blob's hue at full brightness, radius and strength are presentation defaults; neither measures real emission or falloff.",
    "The cookie is a screen-space tint texture, not light transport: everything under a pool gets the same tint."
